# Default Google Sheet (single source of truth)

Unless the user pastes a **different** spreadsheet URL, always read and write
this project's Google Sheet.

## Where to change the sheet (ONE file)

Edit **`sf-deploy/scripts/sheet_config.py`** → `DEFAULT_SPREADSHEET_ID`.

That is the only place that stores the ID. Pipeline scripts default to it.
Do **not** paste a new ID into rules, skills, or other scripts.

Also update `DEFAULT_SPREADSHEET_TITLE` in the same file if the workbook name
changed.

## Required behavior

1. When the user says "the sheet" / "read the sheet" / fetch / validate / deploy
   without a URL, read `sheet_config.py` and use `DEFAULT_SPREADSHEET_ID`.
2. Use that ID for Google Workspace MCP (`get_spreadsheet_info`,
   `read_sheet_values`) and for all `sf-deploy/scripts/*.py` calls.
3. `--spreadsheet-id` / `--sheet-id` is **optional**. Omit it to use the default.
4. If the user pastes a different spreadsheet URL, use that URL for **this task
   only**. Do not change `sheet_config.py` unless they ask to make it the new
   default.
5. Tab scope is unchanged: still confirm which object tab(s) before fetching
   when the target is ambiguous.
